  "raw_text_summary": "For creators looking to efficiently transform long-form videos into engaging short-form content for platforms like YouTube Shorts, TikTok, and Instagram Reels, several AI-powered tools stand out. These tools leverage artificial intelligence to identify key moments, transcribe audio, generate captions, and reformat videos for vertical viewing, significantly streamlining the content creation workflow.\n\nLeading AI tools for creating shorts from long videos include:\n\n*   **OpusClip** is widely recognized for its ability to convert long videos into short clips, automatically identifying the most shareable moments. It reframes videos to a 9:16 vertical aspect ratio, adds captions, and even provides a \"Virality Score\" to predict engagement. OpusClip accepts uploads up to 10 GB and 10 hours long, or links from platforms like YouTube, Vimeo, Zoom, and Google Drive.\n    *   **URL:** opus.pro\n\n*   **CapCut** is a popular choice for creators who have existing video footage and need a fast way to edit for short-form platforms. Its AI-powered features include automatic caption generation, templates, effects, and quick editing tools that help prepare videos for social media. CapCut's long-to-short video tool can automatically transform lengthy videos into concise, engaging shorts with a single click, identifying key moments based on visual, audio, and contextual changes.\n    *   **URL:** capcut.com\n\n*   **Choppity** is an AI tool specifically designed to turn long-form content into short clips automatically. Users can paste a link or upload a file, and the AI transcribes the video, finds standalone short-form moments, trims them to complete thoughts, reframes to 9:16, and adds animated captions. It's suitable for podcasts, webinars, interviews, lectures, and livestreams.\n    *   **URL:** choppity.com\n\n*   **Veed.io** offers AI-powered features for faster content production, including turning podcasts, webinars, and YouTube videos into captioned short clips. Its AI Auto Edits feature can quickly prepare a video for social media by analyzing content, adjusting aspect ratios, cleaning audio, adding B-roll, and auto-captioning.\n    *   **URL:** veed.io\n\n*   **BIGVU** provides an AI short video generator that automatically creates TikToks, Reels, and YouTube Shorts from long videos. Users upload their content, and the AI detects engaging segments, trims them into short clips, and optimizes them for vertical platforms.\n    *   **URL:** bigvu.tv\n\n*   **Adobe Express** includes an AI long-to-short video converter, known as the Clip Maker, which highlights key moments and extracts compelling hooks to produce engaging short-form videos. It allows users to upload videos, apply AI-generated subtitles, customize with branding and animation, and add royalty-free soundtracks.\n    *   **URL:** adobe.com/express\n\nOther notable tools that offer similar capabilities include **Munch**, which differentiates itself with social trend matching to suggest clips aligning with trending audio and formats, and **Canva**, which uses AI to scan long clips for key moments with \"Highlights\" or cohesively split them into shorter cuts with \"Auto-trim\" (Pro features).\n\nThe \"best\" tool often depends on specific user needs, such as the volume of content, desired level of automation, customization options,",
